-- ============================================================
-- Lacerating Shot: RAP coefficient
-- ============================================================

-- DurationIndex 1 = 10000 ms and EffectAmplitude1 = 2000 gives 5 ticks, so the
-- 18% of ranged attack power over the DoT is 0.18 / 5 = 0.036 per tick.  This mirrors
-- Serpent Sting exactly, whose comment in core reads
-- '$RAP*0.2 / number of ticks' for 0.04 over 15000/3000 = 5 ticks.
--
-- RAP rather than melee AP is selected in Unit::SpellDamageBonusDone
-- (Unit.cpp:8878) because SpellFamilyName = 9 alone satisfies
-- SpellInfo::IsRangedWeaponSpell (SpellInfo.cpp:1310) and DamageClass = 3 is
-- not SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_MELEE.  EquippedItemClass 2 / 262156 is belt-and-braces
-- on the same predicate, and additionally requires a ranged weapon.
--
-- EffectBasePoints1 = 0 with EffectDieSides1 = 0 makes this a pure-coefficient
-- DoT: SpellInfo.cpp:433 adds nothing when randomPoints is 0.  That is why the
-- tooltip uses ${$RAP*0.036} rather than $s1 -- $s1 would render 1, since
-- CalcValue is BasePoints + max(1, DieSides), and the client has no knowledge
-- of spell_bonus_data.
--
-- Note the column is `comments`, not `comment`.
DELETE FROM `spell_bonus_data` WHERE `entry` IN (1513, 14326, 14327);
INSERT INTO `spell_bonus_data` (`entry`, `direct_bonus`, `dot_bonus`, `ap_bonus`, `ap_dot_bonus`, `comments`) VALUES
(1513,  0, 0, 0, 0.036, 'Hunter - Lacerating Shot ($RAP*0.18 / 5 ticks)'),
(14326, 0, 0, 0, 0.036, 'Hunter - Lacerating Shot ($RAP*0.18 / 5 ticks)'),
(14327, 0, 0, 0, 0.036, 'Hunter - Lacerating Shot ($RAP*0.18 / 5 ticks)');

-- Ranks 2 and 3 are deliberately identical clones of rank 1.  The ability scales
-- purely off ranged attack power, so there is nothing for a higher rank to
-- improve.  They are kept rather than removed so the existing trainer chain
-- (trainer_spell gates 14326 behind ReqAbility1 = 1513, and 14327 behind 14326)
-- and any character who already knows a higher rank keep working unchanged.
--
-- Category 33 is shared by all three ranks and is retained on purpose: a single
-- CategoryRecoveryTime = 10000 therefore gives the 10s cooldown regardless of
-- which rank a character happens to have.  RecoveryTime stays 0.
--
-- SpellFamilyFlags1 0x10000 (the Scare Beast family bit) is zeroed so Glyph of
-- Scare Beast (58234 / 58298) and anything else keyed to that mask no longer
-- matches -- the spell is no longer a fear.

-- SpellVisual1 336 -> 200002.  336 is Scare Beast's own visual and carries
-- StateKit 4031, the persistent fear swirl the client draws on the target for
-- the aura's entire duration -- unmistakably a fear, on a bleed.  200002 is a
-- custom row added by build_dbc.py: Steady Shot's arrow missile (model 528,
-- bowstring sound 3013) with the blood-splash impact kit 220 that Rend, Deep
-- Wounds and Garrote use, and no StateKit at all.  No retail bleed sets one.

-- CastingTimeIndex 16 (1500 ms) -> 18, NOT 1.  Index 18 is -1000000 ms in
-- SpellCastTimes.dbc, the "ranged special" marker every instant hunter shot
-- uses: Arcane Shot, Serpent Sting and Aimed Shot are all 18.  It is not merely
-- cosmetic.  SpellInfo::CalcCastTime (SpellInfo.cpp:2758) reads
--
--     castTime = CastTimeEntry->CastTime;
--     if (HasAttribute(SPELL_ATTR0_USES_RANGED_SLOT) && !IsAutoRepeatRangedSpell())
--         castTime += 500;
--     return (castTime > 0) ? castTime : 0;
--
-- so with index 1 (0 ms) and Attributes bit 0x2 set, the spell picks up a real
-- 500 ms cast bar and the client plays the generic cast animation instead of
-- the bow/gun shoot animation.  -1000000 clamps to 0 and gives a true instant.
-- (Multi-Shot genuinely is index 1 -- it has a 0.5s cast in 3.3.5a.  That is
-- the same mechanism, not a counter-example.)

-- Damage: 0.18 total RAP (ap_dot_bonus 0.036 per tick), pitched deliberately
-- just under Serpent Sting so the specs can pull it in different directions
-- through talents rather than it arriving pre-tuned for one of them.
--
--   Serpent Sting (r12)   0.040 RAP/tick   0.200 total over 15s
--   Lacerating Shot       0.036 RAP/tick   0.180 total over 10s
--
-- Below on both the per-tick number and the per-application total, which are
-- the two figures a player actually reads off a tooltip.
--
-- The one place it is NOT below is damage per second: 10s of duration on a 10s
-- cooldown is 100% uptime, so 0.18/10s = 0.0180 RAP/sec against Serpent Sting's
-- 0.200/15s = 0.0133 -- about 35% higher, purely from the shorter window.  That
-- is inherent to the duration and cannot be fixed by the coefficient without
-- pushing the visible numbers well below Serpent Sting.  If sustained output
-- needs to be under Serpent Sting too, the coefficient is 0.024/tick (0.12
-- total); the cleaner lever is the 10s cooldown.
--
-- This is the second retune.  The original spec of 300% of RAP was implemented
-- correctly -- the coefficient is per-tick, exactly as Serpent Sting's
-- 0.04 = 0.2/5 is -- it was simply 15x Serpent Sting's total and 3x Arcane
-- Shot's sustained throughput from a single 10s-cooldown button.

-- Auto Shot: ModalNextSpell 0 -> 75.
-- This is what makes a shot start auto-shot, and it is the only reason
-- Lacerating Shot and Instinctive Fire did not.  Neither INITIATE_COMBAT flag
-- is involved -- Arcane Shot has AttributesEx 0 and AttributesEx2 0x20000 and
-- sets neither 0x200 (ATTR1) nor 0x100000 (ATTR2).  Every real hunter shot
-- (Arcane Shot, Serpent Sting, Multi-Shot, Aimed Shot) carries
-- ModalNextSpell = 75 instead, spell 75 being Auto Shot.  Found by diffing all
-- 234 columns against 1978/3044 rather than by guessing at attribute bits.
--
-- Two more columns came out of that same diff and are set for the same reason:
--   AttributesEx2 0 -> 131072  SPELL_ATTR2_DO_NOT_RESET_COMBAT_TIMERS.  Every
--                              hunter shot has it; without it, firing this
--                              clips the auto-shot swing timer.
--   FacingCasterFlags 0 -> 1   must face the target, as all shots require.
--
-- ProcFlags 664232 -> 0.  That value is genuine retail Scare Beast data (the
-- take-damage flags that let a fear break early), not corruption.  It is inert
-- with no spell_proc row, but it has no business on a bleed.
